WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
Meet a virus for the first time, and the
antibody in your blood creeps up slowly,

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:06.530
over days.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.230
In this example, it peaks
14 days after exposure,

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.840
at a low level.

5
00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.460
Meet the same antigen again,
and the rise starts sooner,

6
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.770
and peaks 10 times higher.

7
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.010
What changed inside you, between
the first meeting and the second?

8
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.790
In this mission, you'll
follow both responses,

9
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:27.370
from the first exposure to the second.

10
00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.160
Then you'll read the
antibody data in detail,

11
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:33.270
and compare how long each response lasts.

12
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.960
Your mission: find out what changed
inside you after the first infection.
